      RESIDUE| # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
      RESIDUE| # Merged 2026-09-12 (post-alpha/agent-surface-integration -> post-alpha/integration).
      RESIDUE| # The entry list below is the machine-checked UNION of the two parents' entry sets:
      RESIDUE| #   150 (this branch) u 166 (agent-surface) = 216 entries, 0 lost, 0 extra,
      RESIDUE| # asserted in python against BOTH parents' entry sets - an ENTRY union, never a line
      RESIDUE| # union. The other programme's per-entry annotations for its own registrations are kept
      RESIDUE| # above their entries. Its 12-line header is NOT carried: its `Regenerate with` command
      RESIDUE| # is based on `origin/master` and does not describe this file, and the two notes it adds
      RESIDUE| # (the vendored trees excluded on purpose, the lcov anchoring) are already stated in the
      RESIDUE| # header above. The 21 entries that programme registered by hand are kept, with the
      RESIDUE| # reasons it wrote beside them, because it registered them on purpose so the fork-scoped
      RESIDUE| # ratchets measure them ("Registered as fork-NEW so the fork-scoped ratchets measure
      RESIDUE| # them"): 11 tests/*.py harnesses and 10 tests/src/core/*.{cpp,h} sources. Running the
      RESIDUE| # command under "Regenerate with" reproduces post-alpha/integration's 150 entries exactly,
      RESIDUE| # and prints 195 of this union's 216 - it omits exactly the 21 hand-registered entries and
      RESIDUE| # adds none, which is the same relationship the other programme's own file already had to
      RESIDUE| # its own command (its 166 entries were 21 wider than the 145 that command printed).
      RESIDUE| # This is a deliberate scope decision, recorded here rather than taken
      RESIDUE| # silently: it widens the fork-scoped file-length / complexity / duplication ratchets onto
      RESIDUE| # those files, which is what registering them was for; it narrows no scope this branch had.
      RESIDUE| # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
      RESIDUE| # ---- Agent control surface: automation + scripting command groups ----
      RESIDUE| # Lane post-alpha/cmd-automation off post-alpha/cmd-plugins. The automation.*
      RESIDUE| # group (read-back, the point edits, and the registered-but-refused
      RESIDUE| # automation.mode_set, because this tree has no automation modes) and the
      RESIDUE| # script.* group (script.run drives the embedded ScriptEngine in the running
      RESIDUE| # instance; script.list reports the scripts the build ships). Registered as
      RESIDUE| # fork-NEW so the fork-scoped ratchets measure them.
      RESIDUE| include/ControlAutomationSupport.h
      RESIDUE| # ---- Agent control surface: plugin/dsp + settings command groups ----
      RESIDUE| # Lane post-alpha/cmd-plugins off post-alpha/agent-control-surface. The device
      RESIDUE| # catalogue and device support shared by plugin.list / dsp.get_state, the
      RESIDUE| # plugin.* device+parameter+state+preset commands, and the settings.*/audio.*/
      RESIDUE| # midi.*/app.* group. Registered as fork-NEW so the fork-scoped ratchets measure
      RESIDUE| # them.
      RESIDUE| include/ControlDeviceSupport.h
      RESIDUE| # ---- Notes / clips / tracks command group (SPEC A11-A16, lane post-alpha/cmd-notes) ----
      RESIDUE| # The piano-roll and song-editor half of AGENT-TOOLING.md section 5: note.*,
      RESIDUE| # roll.get_state, clip.*, track.add/remove/rename/set_mute/set_solo/set_arm and
      RESIDUE| # arrangement.get_state, plus the helpers they share. Registered as fork-NEW so
      RESIDUE| # the fork-scoped ratchets measure them.
      RESIDUE| include/ControlEdit.h
